portmixer: fix the build with mingw-w64 headers

- px_win_ds.c: mingw-w64's dsconf.h declares DSPROPSETID_DirectSoundDevice
  and CLSID_DirectSoundPrivate, which conflicts with the file's static
  definitions; give those a PX_ prefix.
- px_win_endpoint.c: <initguid.h> before <endpointvolume.h> makes the SDK
  header define IID_IAudioEndpointVolume, which the file defines itself;
  include it after the SDK headers.
- Pass the out pointers to CoCreateInstance(), IMMDevice_Activate() and
  PaWasapi_GetIMMDevice() as void** (incompatible pointer types are an
  error in current clang and gcc).
- Declare open_ep_mixers_byid() before px_win_wasapi.c calls it.
- px_win_common.c keeps mixer names as char* but called the TCHAR mixer
  API, i.e. the wide one in UNICODE builds, and strdup()ed WCHAR strings
  (truncated names; an error with gcc). Use the ANSI API there.

diff --git a/src/au3wrap/thirdparty/portmixer/src/px_win_common.c b/src/au3wrap/thirdparty/portmixer/src/px_win_common.c
index 14c2e54..59d69c5 100644
--- a/src/au3wrap/thirdparty/portmixer/src/px_win_common.c
+++ b/src/au3wrap/thirdparty/portmixer/src/px_win_common.c
@@ -36,6 +36,11 @@
  *
  */
 
+/* The mixer names are kept as char*: use the ANSI mixer API even in
+   UNICODE builds (strdup() of the wide szName/szPname truncated them). */
+#undef UNICODE
+#undef _UNICODE
+
 #include <windows.h>
 #include <tchar.h>
 
